Ringsmith ER-034 (ruling LuciDin 22 Nov 2026, docs/decomp_recipes.md 3.8)

ee-as for the r5900: no load-delay hazard nop between mfc1 (or another INSN_LOAD_COPROC_DELAY
instruction: cfc1, dmfc1) and the next instruction that uses its general register, when assembled in
reorder mode. In .set noreorder blocks nothing changes (the nop gas emits when gcc's noreorder block
starts stays). The game has 58 mfc1 sites (45 game, 13 SDK) with a normal instruction using the GPR
directly after and none with a nop between; the 11 sites whose user is a branch (gcc's noreorder blocks)
keep the nop. Same form as ee-as_r5900_fpcc_reorder.patch and ee-as_r5900_copmove_reorder.patch; a
documented reconstruction of Sony's assembler behaviour, not Sony's code.

Applies to SSXModding/ps2-ee-toolchain b595ded, directory ee/ (patch -p1 -d <src>/ee), with or without
the other two ee-as patches.

--- a/gas/config/tc-mips.c
+++ b/gas/config/tc-mips.c
@@ -1432,7 +1432,8 @@
       if (! mips_opts.mips16
 	  && mips_opts.isa < 4
 	  && (((prev_pinfo & INSN_LOAD_COPROC_DELAY)
-               && ! cop_interlocks)
+               && ! cop_interlocks
+	       && ! (mips_cpu == 5900 && ! mips_opts.noreorder)) /* Ringsmith ER-034 */
 	      || (! gpr_interlocks
 		  && (prev_pinfo & INSN_LOAD_MEMORY_DELAY))))
 	{
